issue_context.body:
### What is the problem this feature will solve?

While working on the `url-state-machine` (https://github.com/anonrig/url-js), I realized that Node.js/JavaScript lacks the function of casting an array of ASCII numbers to an integer.

<img width="732" alt="raycast-untitled-3" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1935246/165185479-cd88c310-38d3-43cf-ac26-2ded36ccd7da.png">

## JavaScript solution (Number.fromCharCode)

```javascript
function fromCharCode(array, radix) {
  return parseInt(String.fromCharCode(...array), radix)
}
```

## Node.js Solution

```javascript
const assert = require('node:assert/strict');
const { numberFromCharCode } = require('node:util');
assert(numberFromCharCode([49, 50, 51], 10), 123);
```

### What is the feature you are proposing to solve the problem?

Adding `Number.fromCharCode(array, radix)` under Number, and supporting this within Node.js.

### What alternatives have you considered?

Making a proposal to JavaScript TSC.

comments:
I see! I couldn't think of a better function name but something like this would be perfect in my opinion.

```javascript
const assert = require('node:assert/strict');
const { numberFromCharCode } = require('node:util');
assert(numberFromCharCode([49, 50, 51], 10), 123);
```

I don't think an implementation in Node.js core would make it more performance though (Node.js internals are written in JS after all).

If performance is important, I think you'd be better off writing your own util adapted to your use case.

```js
function decimalPositiveIntegerCharCodeToNumber(codes) {
  if (codes.length > 16) throw new Error('number is too big, use BigInt instead');
  let val = 0;
  for(let i = 0; i < codes.length; i++) {
    val += 10 ** i * (codes.at(-i - 1) - 48);
  }
  return val;
}
const buffer = new Uint8Array([49, 50, 51])
console.log(decimalPositiveIntegerCharCodeToNumber(buffer)); // 123
```

There are many ways to convert a buffer to an integer, and it's not particularly clear that your proposal is the true one or the best one.

```js
// 1. OP proposal (radix 10)
Buffer.from(Array.from('123', x => x.codePointAt(0))).toInt(10); // 123
// '1'.repeat(17)? RangeError?

// 2. radix > 10 Uppercase
Buffer.from([0x41, 0x32, 0x33]).toInt(16); // 0xa23
// 0x64? RangeError?

// 3. radix > 10 Lowercase
Buffer.from([0x64, 0x32, 0x33]).toInt(16); // 0xd23
// 0x41? RangeError?

// 4. Ignore leading whitespace like parseInt() ?
Buffer.from([0x20, 0x31, 0x32, 0x33]).toInt(10); // 123

// 5. buf => BigInt(buf.toString('hex'))
Buffer.from([0x31, 0x32, 0x33]).toInt(); // 0x313233n
// LE?

// 6. buf => BigInt(buf.reverse().toString('hex'))
Buffer.from([0x31, 0x32, 0x33]).toInt(); // 0x333231n
// BE?

